# The Prolog backend's facts for native_arithmetic, a knowledge module of
# their own (one set of backend facts per backend; prolog_backend.pl has
# the constructors'): double and even run as the operations natural_double
# and natural_even of lambda_jit_prolog_backend_natives. Trusted, as every
# native is, and vouched for by the comparison of
# tests/native_route_compilation.plt, the_natives_agree_with_their_defines:
# on small naturals the compiled run, which calls the native, reads the
# normal forms the reference reads of the define. The terms bound to natives
# are leaves, so that no round unfolds them and the refinement keeps them as
# written: the JIT calls a native only where the term bound to it stands.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega corpora "library") "native_arithmetic") "native_arithmetic")
λ double even
. export
  ( λ _ rewriting _ _
    . rewriting
    λ _ _ leaves
    . leaves
      ( λk. k even
      + λk. k double
      )
  + λ _ _ _ backend
    . backend
    λ _ natives _ _ _ _
    . natives
      ( λs. s even λk. k "natural_even"
      + λs. s double λk. k "natural_double"
      )
  )
